# Page layout

These are product mandates, not optional UX suggestions.

## The nav names the page

- The in-page heading is screen-reader only (`sr-only`).
- Do not add a visible title or a subtitle under it. Projects and Timer are the reference.

## Pages fill the main column

- App pages fill the main column the way Projects does. Do not cap them with `max-w-*`.
- Auth cards stay narrow.

## Project, client, and activity controls

- A page filter for project, client, or activity uses `Select` from `@/components/ui/select`, the same bordered trigger as the workspace switcher. Include an All row. Text stays left-aligned.
- Assigning those fields on a timer or entry keeps the chips in `EntryMetaChips`.
- Do not use a native `<select>`.
- Every `DropdownMenuItem` and `SelectItem` highlights on hover (`hover:bg-muted`).

## Surfaces separate from the page

- A panel, chart, or table sits on `bg-card` with `border-border`.
- A border alone on the page background is not enough.
